example 1:instance block vs static block
public class Example1 {
    Example1(){
        System.out.println("0-args constructor");
    }
    Example1(int a){
        System.out.println("1-args constructor");
    }
    {
        System.out.println("instance block");
    }
    static {
        System.out.println("static block");
    }


    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Example1();
        new Example1(10);
    }
}

1.static blocks are executed during class loading only once
2.instance block & constructors both are executed during object creation.
but instance block are executed before constructor execution.

 note:
 constructo logics are specific to object but
 instance block logic are common to all objects
 multiple instance block is possible,const,static block,varible posible

 Instance initialization blocks execute every time an object
 is created because they are part of object initialization and run before the constructor.

 ❓ Why instance block executes every time?
 Simple reason:
 👉 Instance block belongs to the object, not the class
 Every time you write:
 new Example1();
 You are saying:
 “Create a NEW object”
 So Java:
 Initializes the object
 Runs all instance initialization code
 Then runs the constructor
 That’s why it executes once per object.

 Key rule to remember 🧠
 🔹 Static block
 Executes ONLY ONCE
 Executes when the class is loaded
 Does not depend on objects

 🔹 Instance block
 Executes EVERY TIME an object is created
 Executes before the constructor
 Is tied to object creation

