🔹 Final instance variable
Must be initialized once per object
Can be initialized using:
Constructor OR
Instance block
Cannot use default values

CASE 1: final instance variable

✅ Valid ways to initialize final instance variable
Option 1: Constructor=>

final int num;
Test() {
    num = 100;
}

Option 2: Instance block
final int num;
{
    num = 100;
}

❌ NOT allowed (assigned twice)
final int num;
{
    num = 50;
}

Test() {
    num = 100; // ❌ error: already initialized
}
__________________________________________________
CASE 2: final static variable
🔹 Final static variable

Must be initialized once per class
Can be initialized using:
Declaration OR
Static block
Cannot be initialized inside constructor
✅ Valid ways to initialize final static
Option 1: At declaration
static final int num = 100;

Option 2: Static block
static final int num;

static {
    num = 100;
}
❌ NOT allowed
static final int num;

Test() {
    num = 100; // ❌ constructor is for objects, not class
}
